The settings are not a separate screen, but appear in a "tray" which is displayed beneath the Header when the user clicks on certain UI elements. This means we can add them to page.tsx directly and don't have to create a temporary page for the new design.

The header now has two states (empty, for when the user encounters it for the first time, and full, for when they have provided some input). The Settings Tray has three states (one for showing global search settings, one for showing hybrid/in-person location settings, and one for showing remote location settings).

