The behaviour is as follows. In the design ("Search Settings 1"):

- When the user first encounters this screen the header should be in "Empty" state.
- The input titled "Input-Keyword" is a text input that fills in search_term in the backend. Clicking on this also reveals the Settings Tray in the Header, set to the "Search Settings" tab.
- Within this tab, the user has the following controls:
- - "Select-Job Sites" - this is a multi-select dropdown menu that allows the user to pick any of the job sites (e.g. Glassdoor, Indeed) supported by JobSpy
- - "Select-Age" - this is a single-select dropdown allowing the user to pick "24 hours", "7 days", or "14 days". This populates hours_old in the backend (so needs to be converted from days to hours)
- - "Input-Include" is text input. The user can provide comma separated terms in quotation marks to supply keywords to include in the job title (replacing the "INCLUDE" section in CONFIG.MD's "FILTERS").
- - "Input-Exclude" is text input. The user can provide comma separated terms in quotation marks to supply keywords to exclude in the job title (replacing the "EXCLUDE" section in CONFIG.MD's "FILTERS").
- - "Input-Blacklist" is a text input. The user can provide comma separated terms in quotation marks to supply employers that should be excluded from search results, replacing the BLACKLIST in CONFIG.MD. 
- - Underneath Input-Blacklist are Blacklist-Suggestions, which are a series of employer names as text links. Clicking on any of these adds that company to the "Input-Blacklist" input field (in quotation marks, as the user would input them) so that they can easily exclude commonly blacklisted employers.

- The input titled Tab-Empty is a button that is a stand-in for the tabs once the user has provide initial input. Clicking on this button shows the Settings Tray on the Location/Hybrid tab.
- Within this tab, the user has the following controls:
- - "Radio-Group-Location-Type" is a radio button group with two options: "Hybrid/In-Person" and "Remote". By default it is set to "Hybrid/In-Person". Selecting "Remote" swaps the Settings Tray tab to the Location/Remote tab - from here, selecting "Hybrid/In-Person" sets it back to the Location/Hybrid tab.
- - On the Location/Hybrid tab, the user has two further controls: "Input-Location" is a text input that allows the user specify the city and country to pass to the search (e.g. "Edinburgh, UK" or "Berlin, Germany") and "Input-Radius", which is a numeric input field for the radius of the search (in km) to pass to the backend. By default this is 0. Once the user has provided a location a tab should be added to the tab bar with this location as the name (not including any characters after the first comma). 
- - On the Location/Remote tab, the user has one control: "Select-Country" is a single-select dropdown control containing a list of countries comptabile with JobSpy's Indeed/Glassdoor search. Once the user has selected a country, a tab should be added to the tab bar with this country as the name. 
- - The user can continue adding additional locations by repeating this process

- Once the user has inputted at least one keyword and at least one location (for Hybrid/In-person) or a country (for Remote) the Button-Search on the Header should be enabled. Clicking on this runs the search (replacing the current "Refresh" button)
- When the user clicks the Button-Search button the Settings Tray should be hidden.
- The user can click on either Input-Keyword or the Button-Add-Location button to display the Settings Tray again (NB: We need to add the ability for users to edit & delete locations later; not for now)

